  "question": {
    "text": "A parallel plate capacitor of area $60 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$ and separation $3 \\mathrm{~mm}$ is charged initially to $90 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$. If the medium between the plate gets slightly conducting and the plate loses the charge initially at the rate of $2.5 \\times 10^{-8} \\mathrm{C} / \\mathrm{s}$, then what is the magnetic field between the plates ?",
    "image": null
